# ZV2 Overbilling Audit Report: June 29-30, 2026

## 1. Executive Summary (OB-5)
This audit report presents the analysis of ZV2 daily network overbilling for June 29 and June 30, 2026. 
The analysis compares actual physical traffic logs (Mastermind) against the active migration states (Zone Move Planner - ZMP) and default cluster-to-zone mappings to identify overbilled traffic.
Overbilled traffic is defined as traffic that was **physically inter-zone** (crossing physical zones, incurring default egress charges) but **logically intra-zone** (where the ZMP target zone matched the source zone, meaning the customer expected it to be free/cheap intra-zone traffic).

